  "prompt": "Griet, the revenue operations lead, needs the MRR bridge for July, August and September 2025 for the board deck: the sales team booked more new and expansion MRR than LedgerLoop's MRR grew, and the board asks where the difference went. Use mrr_monthly: one row per account and month, with the account's MRR in euros on the month's last day, all at one fixed rate; an account with no row in a month had 0 MRR then. For each month, compare each account's MRR at the end of the month with its MRR at the end of the month before. An account with 0 before and MRR now brings all of its MRR now as new_mrr when its first subscription started that month, which is when it has a subscription event with event_type new dated in that month, and as reactivation_mrr otherwise, as an account coming back. An account with MRR in both months brings the rise as expansion_mrr, or the fall as contraction_mrr. An account with MRR before and 0 now brings all of its MRR before as churn_mrr. contraction_mrr and churn_mrr carry a minus sign, so starting_mrr plus the five movements equals ending_mrr to the cent. Return one row for each month from July to September 2025, with eight columns in this order: month, the first day of the month; starting_mrr, the total MRR at the end of the month before; new_mrr; expansion_mrr; reactivation_mrr; contraction_mrr; churn_mrr; and ending_mrr, the total MRR at the end of the month. All amounts are in euros, not rounded, and a movement no account made shows 0. Sort by month from oldest to newest.",
